{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Arial;}}\fs24\b\fs32 VITL Product Snapshot\b0\fs24\parMetaDyn — 2026-04-07\par\par\b Overview\b0\par\tab\bullet\tab VITL is a Unity-based medical simulation product surface on the MetaDyn platform.\par\tab\bullet\tab The current scenario centers on a pediatric infant UTI case where a learner interacts with the infant's concerned mother by text or voice.\par\tab\bullet\tab The current near-term goal is Milestone 1: proving a coherent end-to-end learner loop rather than over-claiming full clinical assessment coverage.\par\par\b Current Product Shape\b0\par\tab\bullet\tab AI delivery layer: MetaDynVoiceController handles learner input, transcription, LLM response flow, text-to-speech, and hidden prompt delivery.\par\tab\bullet\tab Simulation-state layer: VITLSimulationManager owns lifecycle state, activity progression, timers, inactivity escalation, learner-turn storage, and hidden simulation overlay logic.\par\tab\bullet\tab Assessment/intake layer: model-backed communication scoring plus a planned structured patient-history intake flow for Activity 2.\par\par\b Milestone 1 Proof\b0\par\tab\bullet\tab Mother opens with concern.\par\tab\bullet\tab Learner responds by text or voice.\par\tab\bullet\tab Learner communication is scored.\par\tab\bullet\tab Simulation state updates before the mother response.\par\tab\bullet\tab Activity 1 completes through authored thresholds when appropriate.\par\tab\bullet\tab Activity 2 begins as structured patient-history capture.\par\par\b Key Decisions\b0\par\tab\bullet\tab The simulation manager remains the authority for activity progression.\par\tab\bullet\tab Conversation history is not the same thing as structured patient history.\par\tab\bullet\tab The learner-entered intake UI should become the canonical structured history record for Activity 2.\par\tab\bullet\tab Fallback scoring is a resilience mechanism, not the intended long-term assessment layer.\par\tab\bullet\tab Milestone 1 should stay focused and avoid scope creep into full clinical grading, automatic structured extraction from dialogue, or broad event-system rewrites.\par\par\b Immediate Next Steps\b0\par\tab\bullet\tab Lock the canonical Activity 1 to Activity 2 demo path.\par\tab\bullet\tab Define and implement the first pass of VITLPatientIntakeRecord and VITLPatientIntakeController.\par\tab\bullet\tab Add required-fields plus learner-confirmation completion behavior for Activity 2.\par\tab\bullet\tab Add analytics-safe milestone events without over-expanding scope.\par\par}